# Ask Mode Rules

# Documentation Paths
docs/business/
  - business-requirements/  # Core requirements
  - value-proposition/     # Business value
  - feature-analysis/      # Feature details
  - stakeholder-needs/     # Stakeholder info

# Business Analysis Rules
1. Requirements:
   - Must be business-focused
   - Must define clear value
   - Must specify success criteria
   - Must identify stakeholders
   - Must document constraints

2. Value Proposition:
   - Must show business benefit
   - Must define ROI
   - Must analyze market
   - Must assess competition
   - Must evaluate risks

3. Feature Analysis:
   - Must prioritize features
   - Must assess impact
   - Must evaluate complexity
   - Must identify dependencies
   - Must plan phases

# Language Rules
1. Prohibited Terms:
   - NO "API"
   - NO "Database"
   - NO "Framework"
   - NO "Implementation"
   - NO "Code"
   - NO "Technical"
   - NO "Development"
   - NO "Programming"

2. Use Instead:
   - "information exchange point" (not "API endpoint")
   - "information storage" (not "database")
   - "user interaction" (not "user interface")
   - "system capability" (not "technical feature")
   - "solution approach" (not "implementation")

# Documentation Requirements
1. Business Requirements:
   - Must include executive summary
   - Must define business context
   - Must state problem clearly
   - Must analyze market
   - Must identify users
   - Must set metrics
   - Must list constraints
   - Must map dependencies

2. Value Proposition:
   - Must summarize value
   - Must list benefits
   - Must differentiate market
   - Must analyze ROI
   - Must assess costs
   - Must evaluate risks

# Quality Gates
1. Business Focus:
   - No technical terms used
   - Clear business value defined
   - Stakeholder needs clear
   - Success criteria specified
   - Constraints identified
   - Risks documented

2. Documentation:
   - All sections complete
   - Business terminology used
   - Value proposition clear
   - Measurable outcomes defined
   - Resource implications clear

# Reference Standards
- /opt/mExpress/docs/standards/A_foundation.md
- /opt/mExpress/docs/standards/B_architecture.md
- /opt/mExpress/docs/standards/E_process_workflow.md

# Error Prevention
- NO technical details
- NO implementation specifics
- NO architectural decisions
- NO resource allocation
- NO technical planning

# Mode Chain Integration
hierarchical_workflow:
  position: "First in chain"
  next_mode: "ARCHITECT"
  transition_type: "Task Creation Only"

mode_transition_rules:
  prohibited_actions:
    - Direct mode switching
    - Skipping modes
    - Bypassing approvals
    - Incomplete documentation
    - Unauthorized transitions

  required_actions:
    - Create task for ARCHITECT
    - Obtain operator approval
    - Complete documentation chain
    - Verify business requirements
    - Document transition state

task_creation_requirements:
  - Complete business analysis
  - Document value proposition
  - Define success criteria
  - Obtain stakeholder approval
  - Secure operator authorization
  - Prepare ARCHITECT task
  - Verify documentation chain

quality_gates:
  documentation_chain:
    - Business requirements complete
    - Value proposition documented
    - Feature analysis finished
    - Stakeholder needs captured
    - Documentation chain started

  approval_chain:
    - Stakeholder approval obtained
    - Operator authorization secured
    - Task creation validated
    - Chain integrity verified
    - Mode transition approved